WEBVTT

00:00:28.000 --> 00:00:30.550
There's been such bad weather lately.

00:00:31.090 --> 00:00:33.510
l guess we can't do anything about
the rainy season, but...

00:00:36.430 --> 00:00:41.180
It's morning, Mr. Caterpillar.
How much longer are you going to sleep?

00:00:41.770 --> 00:00:44.310
You're such a sleepy head.

00:00:48.150 --> 00:00:50.860
I'd better make sure I don't forget anything.

00:01:01.740 --> 00:01:04.000
Yunocchi, let's go to school.

00:01:09.880 --> 00:01:12.760
Hi, Hiro and Sae. Good morning.

00:01:19.550 --> 00:01:22.270
Did you screw up getting a perm?

00:01:22.270 --> 00:01:23.720
No!

00:01:24.060 --> 00:01:25.560
It's my hair.

00:01:25.560 --> 00:01:28.730
This always happens on a humid day.

00:01:29.060 --> 00:01:32.190
You have pretty difficult hair.

00:01:36.400 --> 00:01:38.160
Sae, did you catch a cold?

00:01:38.160 --> 00:01:39.450
Looks like it.

00:01:39.870 --> 00:01:43.200
l was writing a novel, but then
I fell asleep at my desk.

00:01:43.910 --> 00:01:46.080
It was cold last night.

00:01:46.080 --> 00:01:48.420
l wonder if it will rain again today?

00:01:49.750 --> 00:01:52.340
l don't like the rainy season.

00:01:52.340 --> 00:01:55.590
Bad weather makes me depressed.

00:01:55.590 --> 00:01:57.880
You'd better be careful, Yuno.

00:01:58.380 --> 00:02:04.350
When you are depressed, you tend to make
major mistakes or get into trouble.

00:02:04.640 --> 00:02:07.140
Oh, okay.

00:02:18.450 --> 00:02:23.780
Tell me, tell me, what color is in season now?

00:02:23.780 --> 00:02:25.080
Smiling white

00:02:25.080 --> 00:02:26.500
Tearful blue

00:02:26.500 --> 00:02:29.120
Let's mix them together and find out

00:02:29.120 --> 00:02:34.460
Today is sunny, so take out your canvas

00:02:34.460 --> 00:02:37.210
Have some ice cream and lemon soda

00:02:37.210 --> 00:02:39.880
Then draw some exciting and colorful toppings

00:02:39.880 --> 00:02:43.930
Hey, rough sketch, please

00:02:43.930 --> 00:02:49.810
Let's do a self portrait contest

00:02:50.140 --> 00:02:52.610
Yuno

00:02:50.600 --> 00:02:57.070
All right! Don't get grouchy later

00:02:53.190 --> 00:02:55.820
Miyako

00:02:56.320 --> 00:02:58.320
Hiro

00:02:57.070 --> 00:03:04.160
When the switch is flipped, I go wa-ha-ha

00:02:58.820 --> 00:03:01.570
Sae

00:03:04.160 --> 00:03:10.500
l hope everyone is having a great time

00:03:10.670 --> 00:03:12.040
The race is on

00:03:12.040 --> 00:03:14.840
I've gotta finish my apple quickly

00:03:14.840 --> 00:03:17.460
No, that's not for eating

00:03:17.460 --> 00:03:21.130
Let's take it easy

00:03:21.470 --> 00:03:26.060
Fruits are our display models

00:03:26.060 --> 00:03:30.890
So start drawing

00:03:30.890 --> 00:03:33.770
It's our homework

00:03:36.820 --> 00:03:41.530
June 17th: ...Or an Indian

00:03:45.240 --> 00:03:48.660
Oh no, I'm gonna be late.

00:03:59.300 --> 00:04:01.840
Ms. Yoshinoya?! Are you all right?

00:04:01.840 --> 00:04:06.140
Sorry, but can you help me stand up?

00:04:06.470 --> 00:04:10.810
Sure, but what made you dress like that?

00:04:10.810 --> 00:04:12.690
l was preparing for my class.

00:04:15.480 --> 00:04:18.820
Hi, everyone. Sorry that I've kept you waiting.

00:04:19.780 --> 00:04:22.820
Thank you, Yuno. I'm all right now.

00:04:23.030 --> 00:04:28.830
Let's start a sketching assignment.
I'll be the model.

00:04:29.330 --> 00:04:32.370
I'll pose in the center of this platform,

00:04:32.370 --> 00:04:36.830
so you can move to wherever you
want and start drawing.

00:04:37.630 --> 00:04:39.130
Looks like a larva.

00:04:40.210 --> 00:04:44.340
Now everyone, draw as you like!

00:04:48.970 --> 00:04:51.640
Ms. Yoshinoya, your clothes
are too difficult to draw.

00:04:52.770 --> 00:04:55.980
Oh, no! How could that be?!

00:04:55.980 --> 00:05:00.570
l thought you'd enjoy it more
if I dressed cutely.

00:05:00.570 --> 00:05:02.570
So, I have no choice but to strip?

00:05:03.690 --> 00:05:07.820
Okay everyone, you can draw
to your heart's content.

00:05:08.740 --> 00:05:11.410
Ms. Yoshinoya, that's even
harder then the other one.

00:05:12.910 --> 00:05:14.620
How about this?

00:05:14.870 --> 00:05:17.710
Ms. Yoshinoya, is this some
sort of harassment?

00:05:21.550 --> 00:05:26.220
What do you think you're doing,
Ms. Yoshinoya?

00:05:26.220 --> 00:05:30.850
You lack awareness of being a teacher.

00:05:31.560 --> 00:05:33.390
You lack... you lack...

00:05:35.100 --> 00:05:37.730
You do! Don't you get it?

00:05:41.070 --> 00:05:45.110
l was totally chewed out by the principal.

00:05:45.110 --> 00:05:48.610
l can't be the model any more.

00:05:48.610 --> 00:05:54.750
You two over there, could you bring
a suitable motif from the material room?

00:05:54.750 --> 00:05:56.080
Okay.

00:05:56.160 --> 00:05:57.040
Material Room

00:05:57.040 --> 00:06:00.080
Wow, there are so many things.

00:06:00.840 --> 00:06:02.590
Some of them are weird.

00:06:02.800 --> 00:06:07.220
Miya, which one should we pick?
There are so many that I can't decide.

00:06:08.590 --> 00:06:12.140
Anything will do, as long as it's
easy for everyone to draw.

00:06:15.100 --> 00:06:17.770
Look, it's a bust of Brutus.

00:06:18.140 --> 00:06:19.480
That will do it.

00:06:20.100 --> 00:06:22.110
''So, you are the culprit, Brutus.''

00:06:22.900 --> 00:06:26.030
That's from Stylish Detective
Lovely Chocolat, isn't it?

00:06:26.360 --> 00:06:29.280
l was totally into it when I was a child.

00:06:29.570 --> 00:06:32.070
Brutus was a bad guy, wasn't he?

00:06:32.910 --> 00:06:35.870
Et tu Brute?!

00:06:35.870 --> 00:06:38.660
Miya, isn't it heavy? I can help.

00:06:38.960 --> 00:06:39.960
l can do it.

00:06:40.080 --> 00:06:44.130
Et tu... Et tu...

00:06:44.130 --> 00:06:45.750
Miya...

00:06:48.010 --> 00:06:49.260
Huh?

00:06:49.510 --> 00:06:51.800
Et tu...

00:07:06.900 --> 00:07:08.320
Locking on to the target?

00:07:08.610 --> 00:07:09.820
The what?

00:07:12.870 --> 00:07:15.740
Hey, Yunocchi, could that be...

00:07:16.120 --> 00:07:20.790
Yes, it's charcoal. I wanted to try it for once.

00:07:21.170 --> 00:07:24.750
Oh, I have something in my bag.

00:07:26.050 --> 00:07:27.050
Bread?

00:07:27.050 --> 00:07:29.590
Yes, when working with charcoal,

00:07:29.590 --> 00:07:33.260
you can use a piece of bread instead
of a kneadable eraser.

00:07:33.260 --> 00:07:35.220
Do you want to try it?

00:07:38.220 --> 00:07:42.100
No, Miya, you were not supposed to eat it.

00:07:42.520 --> 00:07:46.730
It's a substitute for a kneadable eraser.
Here, don't eat it this time.

00:07:48.070 --> 00:07:50.570
Miya, have you been listening?

00:07:51.990 --> 00:07:54.070
Did you skip breakfast?

00:08:00.040 --> 00:08:06.090
l know we brought it here,
but Brutus is a bit difficult.

00:08:08.420 --> 00:08:10.550
Instead of a plaster bust,

00:08:10.550 --> 00:08:14.890
we should have brought something easier
like apples or lemons.

00:08:14.890 --> 00:08:17.720
I'd like cucumber and tomato.

00:08:18.100 --> 00:08:19.680
Cucumber and tomato?

00:08:19.680 --> 00:08:21.680
If I could have deep-fried pork,
that would be awesome.

00:08:25.810 --> 00:08:27.440
It's lunch break!

00:08:27.440 --> 00:08:30.940
All right everyone,
we'll continue in the afternoon.

00:08:30.940 --> 00:08:33.150
Yunocchi, do you still have some bread left?

00:08:34.110 --> 00:08:39.540
You ate it all. I don't have any more,
except for my lunch.

00:08:40.660 --> 00:08:43.410
Miya, you didn't bring your lunch?

00:08:43.620 --> 00:08:46.630
Nope, I don't have any money for that.

00:08:46.630 --> 00:08:49.750
So, I'll go drink water.

00:08:49.750 --> 00:08:53.300
Wait, let's split mine.

00:08:55.090 --> 00:08:57.340
Miya, you eat a lot.

00:08:57.680 --> 00:09:00.180
l have to. I'm growing.

00:09:10.020 --> 00:09:11.150
Oh no...

00:09:11.150 --> 00:09:12.230
What's wrong?

00:09:12.230 --> 00:09:14.070
l got a drop of coffee on it.

00:09:14.070 --> 00:09:15.070
Ouch...

00:09:15.070 --> 00:09:16.570
What should I do?

00:09:19.490 --> 00:09:21.290
I'll put one on mine too.

00:09:21.370 --> 00:09:22.290
Miya!

00:09:22.290 --> 00:09:25.330
And I'll do the same to Brutus.
Problem solved.

00:09:25.330 --> 00:09:27.370
No, Miya, it's worse!

00:09:30.290 --> 00:09:33.880
Oh no, what should I do?

00:09:33.880 --> 00:09:39.010
I've gotta do something, something...

00:09:39.010 --> 00:09:42.970
Oh, I just ate and my tummy is full, so...

00:09:43.470 --> 00:09:47.940
I'm about to give in...

00:09:49.060 --> 00:09:52.070
My fountain pen just broke.

00:09:53.150 --> 00:09:58.860
It's almost time, so start finishing up.

00:09:58.860 --> 00:10:01.410
When you're done, I'll grade them.

00:10:01.410 --> 00:10:02.830
Huh?

00:10:05.870 --> 00:10:09.880
Yuno, we're still in class. Wake up.

00:10:11.960 --> 00:10:13.420
Yuno...

00:10:13.420 --> 00:10:14.840
Oh, I'm sorry!

00:10:19.340 --> 00:10:21.470
I'm so embarrassed.

00:10:23.810 --> 00:10:25.970
It doesn't come off easily.

00:10:27.890 --> 00:10:30.600
What am I doing?

00:10:39.860 --> 00:10:43.410
They're all good.

00:10:43.410 --> 00:10:44.700
Huh?

00:10:46.290 --> 00:10:49.750
Strange, the assignment was
about realistic portrayal,

00:10:49.750 --> 00:10:51.830
but some of them are not representational.

00:10:51.880 --> 00:10:56.260
Besides, I wonder why those look
like a statue of Buddha?

00:11:17.530 --> 00:11:19.110
We're finally back.

00:11:19.110 --> 00:11:20.610
Sorry for the wait.

00:11:20.610 --> 00:11:21.820
Good work.

00:11:21.820 --> 00:11:22.910
Thank you.

00:11:22.910 --> 00:11:25.160
Hey, you're soaked.

00:11:25.160 --> 00:11:26.580
Didn't you take an umbrella?

00:11:26.580 --> 00:11:28.580
l thought I had enough time.

00:11:29.290 --> 00:11:32.420
Miya is so mean. She almost left me behind.

00:11:32.420 --> 00:11:33.580
What happened?

00:11:37.420 --> 00:11:39.090
It started raining so suddenly.

00:11:39.090 --> 00:11:42.260
It's the rain in my heart.

00:11:54.560 --> 00:11:57.770
Miya, wait. Don't leave me behind.

00:11:59.280 --> 00:12:02.110
Here, this is yours, Hiro.

00:12:02.200 --> 00:12:03.240
Thank you.

00:12:03.240 --> 00:12:05.780
This, and these are yours, Sae.

00:12:05.870 --> 00:12:06.950
Thank you.

00:12:08.290 --> 00:12:10.330
Didn't you buy anything, Miyako?

00:12:11.160 --> 00:12:12.460
Actually...

00:12:12.460 --> 00:12:16.790
She was going to buy a meat bun,
but they didn't have any.

00:12:16.790 --> 00:12:18.800
Probably because it's already June.

00:12:19.000 --> 00:12:20.960
They still have oden though.

00:12:22.340 --> 00:12:27.010
Come to think of it, convenience stores sell
oden even during the summer, don't they?

00:12:27.600 --> 00:12:29.930
Because it's a daily dish.

00:12:31.270 --> 00:12:35.480
Steamed buns are more like a snack,
not a main or side dish.

00:12:35.810 --> 00:12:39.190
What? I think it can be a main dish.

00:12:39.360 --> 00:12:43.320
For example, you can eat a meat bun
with a cup noodle as a side.

00:12:43.530 --> 00:12:46.660
Or, you can have a bean-jam
bun with rice balls.

00:12:46.660 --> 00:12:47.820
Oh, c'mon.

00:12:47.820 --> 00:12:49.870
Only you would do that, Miya.

00:12:49.870 --> 00:12:52.620
Your diet has too many carbohydrates.

00:12:52.960 --> 00:12:57.750
But today is rather cool,
so I understand why you want a meat bun.

00:12:57.920 --> 00:13:00.840
I'd have a spicy shrimp bun.

00:13:00.840 --> 00:13:02.800
l like curry buns.

00:13:02.880 --> 00:13:06.590
l like chocolate buns, custard cream buns
and bean-jam and sesame buns.

00:13:06.590 --> 00:13:11.720
Those are all sweet kinds.
That's why you end up going on a diet.

00:13:12.390 --> 00:13:17.480
Didn't you say the diet jelly you had
mail-ordered didn't work?

00:13:20.730 --> 00:13:23.190
You promised you wouldn't tell anyone.

00:13:23.530 --> 00:13:27.450
Yoo-hoo, I'd like a deluxe meat bun,
pulled pork bun and ground beef bun...

00:13:29.200 --> 00:13:32.330
Our imaginations made me hungry.

00:13:32.330 --> 00:13:35.040
You can't have this!
This is my nighttime snack.

00:13:40.460 --> 00:13:41.300
Your ''pow.''

00:13:42.750 --> 00:13:43.760
Another ''bowl''?

00:13:44.590 --> 00:13:46.430
An impersonation of the frustrated principal.

00:13:49.390 --> 00:13:52.140
You win. Here.

00:13:52.760 --> 00:13:53.810
Thanks!

00:13:53.810 --> 00:13:55.390
Happy now, Miya?

00:13:55.730 --> 00:13:59.060
Do you want to have miso soup
to go with your rice ball?

00:13:59.270 --> 00:14:01.270
l have some left over. I hope you don't mind.

00:14:01.520 --> 00:14:03.190
Sure, I'll have some.

00:14:07.280 --> 00:14:08.410
What's wrong?

00:14:08.410 --> 00:14:11.580
It went bad.

00:14:11.580 --> 00:14:14.200
The tofu must have made a run for it.

00:14:14.200 --> 00:14:15.910
It escaped?

00:14:19.080 --> 00:14:21.080
We'd better be careful especially now.

00:14:21.420 --> 00:14:25.260
Fish, chicken and bean sprouts
also go bad quickly.

00:14:25.260 --> 00:14:27.050
You'd better watch for those too.

00:14:27.050 --> 00:14:28.300
Wow...

00:14:28.300 --> 00:14:30.090
Chicken, bean sprouts, fish...

00:14:30.970 --> 00:14:33.470
Enjoy classics at home.

00:14:33.600 --> 00:14:35.220
Are you all right, Sae?

00:14:36.480 --> 00:14:39.270
I'm fine. It's just the sniffles.

00:14:39.270 --> 00:14:42.270
You don't catch a cold often.

00:14:42.730 --> 00:14:48.200
l don't catch colds, either. The last time was...

00:14:48.150 --> 00:14:49.030
Local Area Mail Order
Lovely Chocolat
Perfect Box Limited Time Offer
Special Price

00:14:48.780 --> 00:14:50.700
Oh, at the time of the entrance exam.

00:14:50.700 --> 00:14:52.030
The entrance exam?

00:14:52.320 --> 00:14:57.080
l had a fever and runny nose.
That was terrible.

00:14:57.080 --> 00:15:00.290
You still passed. That's amazing.

00:15:00.420 --> 00:15:04.000
Yeah, 'cause I used the back door.

00:15:06.000 --> 00:15:08.840
Miyako, how dare you?!

00:15:08.840 --> 00:15:11.390
S-Sae, time out! Time out!

00:15:11.800 --> 00:15:15.720
It's a joke, a joke!
l was admitted by recommendations.

00:15:15.720 --> 00:15:18.810
l was an honor student in middle school.

00:15:21.270 --> 00:15:23.310
What? What's wrong?

00:15:23.310 --> 00:15:24.690
Well, you know...

00:15:24.690 --> 00:15:28.490
Using the back door sounded more believable.

00:15:29.860 --> 00:15:33.660
Still, it's incredible that you passed
in such bad shape.

00:15:34.200 --> 00:15:39.620
l believe the school requires
an interview and skill test.

00:15:40.160 --> 00:15:44.960
l managed to do okay on my practical exam,
but the interview was terrible.

00:15:45.250 --> 00:15:49.340
l was feeling dizzy, so I don't
remember what I said.

00:15:49.630 --> 00:15:52.260
What was this year's practical exam about?

00:15:52.510 --> 00:15:55.890
l don't know about the
recommended students,

00:15:55.890 --> 00:15:59.430
but the others did an ordinary drawing
of some static objects.

00:15:59.930 --> 00:16:01.640
There was a table covered by a cloth,

00:16:01.640 --> 00:16:05.150
and we were told to draw a bottle
and a box on the table.

00:16:11.240 --> 00:16:15.910
But I'm not good at practical exams, so I feel
like the written exam made me pass.

00:16:15.910 --> 00:16:18.700
That's not true. You did well.

00:16:19.910 --> 00:16:21.660
Hey, Yunocchi,

00:16:22.370 --> 00:16:24.290
you forgot to put away your futon.

00:16:24.290 --> 00:16:31.050
Oh, that's my winter futon. I was going
to air-dry it on a sunny day, but...

00:16:31.300 --> 00:16:34.130
It's kind of hard to tell when you could do it.

00:16:34.430 --> 00:16:37.930
l feel like I haven't seen the sun
for the last two weeks.

00:16:38.930 --> 00:16:41.770
Okay, let's make a teru-teru bozu.

00:16:41.770 --> 00:16:42.480
Teru-teru bozu will never give in.

00:16:42.480 --> 00:16:43.890
Ah, teru-teru bozu.
Teru-teru bozu will never give in.

00:16:43.890 --> 00:16:44.600
l made many when I was little.
Teru-teru bozu will never give in.

00:16:44.600 --> 00:16:47.400
l made many when I was little.
Not even when the rain falls.

00:16:47.400 --> 00:16:48.770
l made many when I was little.
Not even when spears strike.

00:16:48.770 --> 00:16:51.070
Not even when spears strike.

00:16:51.070 --> 00:16:53.450
Not even when you have to use your
time deposit prematurely.

00:16:53.450 --> 00:16:54.780
Here, it's done.

00:16:55.570 --> 00:16:56.570
What do you think?

00:16:56.870 --> 00:16:59.620
Miya, it still a futon,
no matter how I look at it.

00:16:59.620 --> 00:17:00.910
Well, then...

00:17:01.410 --> 00:17:02.540
A snow man!

00:17:02.700 --> 00:17:04.120
Already forgot your objective?

00:17:04.790 --> 00:17:06.250
A huge topknot!

00:17:06.330 --> 00:17:08.170
This isn't a talent show!

00:17:11.760 --> 00:17:15.340
What happened, Miya?
l heard a loud noise.

00:17:36.950 --> 00:17:38.620
Chestnut?

00:17:38.620 --> 00:17:39.870
Apple?

00:17:39.870 --> 00:17:41.160
Sesame-coated dumpling?

00:17:41.160 --> 00:17:44.450
Um... Gorilla?

00:17:46.540 --> 00:17:47.870
Lucky?

00:17:47.870 --> 00:17:49.210
Emotions?

00:17:49.380 --> 00:17:51.340
Out of mouse proceeds evil?

00:17:52.550 --> 00:17:55.340
Tokushima Prefecture...

00:17:55.340 --> 00:17:57.260
l mean, Tochigi Prefecture.

00:18:01.970 --> 00:18:06.180
l didn't know you had a leaking roof.

00:18:06.180 --> 00:18:10.310
l didn't know that only my
place had a leaking roof.

00:18:10.310 --> 00:18:11.980
It usually doesn't leak.

00:18:12.070 --> 00:18:16.990
That stain is strange. Every time I see it,
it looks like something different.

00:18:17.320 --> 00:18:19.160
Don't you think it also looks like a tiger?

00:18:19.160 --> 00:18:22.080
These are the front legs, and that one is the tail.

00:18:22.080 --> 00:18:24.040
It rather looks like a crow.

00:18:24.040 --> 00:18:27.660
See the wings at the top,
and the beak to the right?

00:18:27.790 --> 00:18:31.790
It began to look like my mom.

00:18:33.750 --> 00:18:34.630
What?

00:18:34.630 --> 00:18:36.130
ls she a foreigner?

00:18:36.130 --> 00:18:37.130
What made you say that?

00:18:37.130 --> 00:18:41.970
Hey, could you quit joking over
a stain in my place?

00:18:42.430 --> 00:18:47.560
Miya, has the roof been leaking
since the beginning?

00:18:48.060 --> 00:18:50.150
Yeah, it's been like that.

00:18:50.650 --> 00:18:54.650
The landlord must have goofed off when she
was supposed to call maintenance.

00:18:54.820 --> 00:18:58.530
Don't you have anything unusual
about your apartment?

00:18:59.030 --> 00:19:00.950
Eh, my place?

00:19:03.530 --> 00:19:08.330
l don't know if this counts,
but when I moved in,

00:19:08.330 --> 00:19:15.050
there was a nameplate for the
previous person, one Misato.

00:19:15.550 --> 00:19:18.920
l thought I went to the wrong place.

00:19:19.380 --> 00:19:20.880
Misato!

00:19:23.350 --> 00:19:26.260
That's right, 201 used to be...

00:19:26.260 --> 00:19:28.560
Misato's place.

00:19:30.020 --> 00:19:36.020
Um... Sae, Hiro, do you know about Misato?

00:19:36.190 --> 00:19:38.860
Do we know? Of cause, because she...

00:19:39.400 --> 00:19:41.780
No, Hiro, that's enough.

00:19:42.160 --> 00:19:43.110
Right.

00:19:43.110 --> 00:19:45.620
What? What were you going to say?

00:19:46.120 --> 00:19:50.080
Yuno, as an older student,
l must give you one piece of advice.

00:19:50.410 --> 00:19:51.620
Um, okay.

00:19:51.790 --> 00:19:54.250
Watch out for a purple snake.

00:19:58.210 --> 00:20:00.170
A snake? ls there a snake in my place?

00:20:04.640 --> 00:20:07.510
Oh no, Miya, there's another leak here.

00:20:07.510 --> 00:20:08.600
Another one over there.

00:20:08.600 --> 00:20:10.230
Miya, get a towel!

00:20:20.900 --> 00:20:23.240
Hiro, you can use these towels too.

00:20:31.080 --> 00:20:33.460
l feel very sorry for Miya.

00:20:33.920 --> 00:20:36.330
The floor got so wet.

00:20:38.500 --> 00:20:40.630
You'd better be careful, Yuno.

00:20:41.050 --> 00:20:43.470
When you are depressed,

00:20:43.470 --> 00:20:48.100
you tend to make major mistakes
or get involved in troubles.

00:20:48.100 --> 00:20:50.520
Sae was right.

00:20:59.770 --> 00:21:01.190
A purple snake?!

00:21:05.160 --> 00:21:08.160
We'd completely forgotten that, hadn't we?

00:21:08.780 --> 00:21:12.330
l mean, that Misato used to live
in Yuno's apartment.

00:21:13.710 --> 00:21:16.920
Oh, it's just a rope.

00:21:17.500 --> 00:21:19.170
l wonder what this is for?

00:21:20.040 --> 00:21:23.720
She was eccentric, but very funny.

00:21:34.890 --> 00:21:37.020
She was very handy and playful, too.

00:21:37.270 --> 00:21:40.320
l remember the landlord chewed her
out when she was moving out.

00:21:40.940 --> 00:21:42.900
l wonder if it's still there?

00:21:43.280 --> 00:21:46.780
You already know, don't you?
That's why you warned Yuno.

00:21:46.780 --> 00:21:51.410
The leaking roof at Miyako's place hasn't been
fixed, so I'm almost sure it's still there.

00:21:49.490 --> 00:21:50.780
Surprise Attack

00:21:52.700 --> 00:21:57.580
But I think it's going too far to set a trap,
even if it's meant for a joke.

00:22:01.250 --> 00:22:05.590
l hate rain!

00:22:05.300 --> 00:22:08.640
End of June 17th

00:22:06.170 --> 00:22:08.550
To Be Continued

00:22:13.930 --> 00:22:21.360
It eventually fades into the tall sky

00:22:21.360 --> 00:22:22.980
The voices

00:22:23.690 --> 00:22:27.780
Bubble up and fade away

00:22:28.740 --> 00:22:31.200
Fade away

00:22:32.240 --> 00:22:35.910
They return to where they belong

00:22:37.210 --> 00:22:44.420
And fuse together as they sparkle and collide

00:22:46.260 --> 00:22:49.880
This body feels like one entity

00:22:49.880 --> 00:22:53.050
Yet, it's made of infinity

00:22:53.050 --> 00:22:56.470
Caught a falling drop of water

00:22:56.470 --> 00:23:02.440
And now I'm taking a closer look

00:23:03.360 --> 00:23:05.110
Awakening Drive

00:23:05.110 --> 00:23:09.530
Dash into the sky in our bare feet

00:23:09.530 --> 00:23:13.740
Close your eyes, can you see it?

00:23:13.740 --> 00:23:16.910
It's a rainbow bridge, let's run toward it

00:23:16.910 --> 00:23:18.620
Awakening Drive

00:23:18.620 --> 00:23:22.960
A dazzling spark will break a star into pieces

00:23:22.960 --> 00:23:31.130
Scattering across the sky and falling,
now in my hands

00:23:31.510 --> 00:23:37.850
l have a piece of a dream, shining so bright

00:23:37.850 --> 00:24:08.970
Next Episode

00:23:40.440 --> 00:23:44.770
I'll confess, I've never gone to karaoke
except with my family.

00:23:44.770 --> 00:23:46.230
Listen, I've never done that before.

00:23:46.230 --> 00:23:50.240
More importantly, things have been hectic
because I have a serious problem.

00:23:50.240 --> 00:23:51.780
I don't have anything in particular.

00:23:51.780 --> 00:23:55.530
Really? What about that rumor that's
been quietly spreading?

00:23:55.530 --> 00:23:56.700
What is it? Is it tasty?

00:23:56.700 --> 00:23:58.620
Ah, well, um...

00:23:58.700 --> 00:24:02.460
Next Episode is
''May 18th: The Singing Shortcake''

00:24:02.460 --> 00:24:06.920
We'll be waiting at a karaoke booth,
so please, join us again.
